INSERT INTO `mx_motor_category` VALUES (1,100,'High / Low Voltage AC & DC Motors','unnamed.jpg','<p>The complete CG Power / Crompton motor portfolio through one authorised channel partner &mdash; high-voltage machines up to 15 MW, low-voltage industrial motors, energy-efficient IE2/IE3/IE4 ranges, hazardous-area certified motors, and DC machines. Bombay Engineering Syndicate has supplied Indian industry from Fort, Mumbai since 1957, with application engineering on every inquiry.</p>\n<p>This family is where plants, utilities, and process industries source their prime movers. Low-voltage motors (up to 1000 V) drive pumps, fans, compressors, conveyors, and machine tools across the 0.37 kW to 630 kW band. High-voltage motors (3.3 kV to 11 kV) power the large fans, mills, and pumps of cement, steel, power, and petrochemical plants. Alongside them sit purpose-built variants: flameproof (Ex d) and increased-safety (Ex e) motors for gas and dust zones, IE4 super-premium motors for energy-conscious sites, and DC motors where a wide speed range and high starting torque matter.</p>\n<p>Selection turns on voltage, kW, speed, frame size, mounting, and enclosure &mdash; plus efficiency class and any ATEX/IECEx hazardous-area certification. Our engineers match the motor to your load and supply genuine, factory-warranted units. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Send an inquiry</a> with your nameplate or duty details for a sized recommendation.</p>',NULL,0,'motor/high-low-voltage-ac-dc-motors','en',NULL,0,1),(5,102,'Safe Area Single Phase AC Motor','unnamed.jpg',NULL,NULL,0,'motor/single-phase-ac-motor/safe-area-single-phase-ac-motor','en',NULL,0,0),(6,102,'Hazardous Area Single Phase AC Motor','unnamed.jpg',NULL,NULL,0,'motor/single-phase-ac-motor/hazardous-area-single-phase-ac-motor','en',NULL,0,0),(7,24,'Laminated Yoke DC Motor','unnamed.jpg',NULL,NULL,0,'motor/dc-motors/laminated-yoke-dc-motor','en',NULL,0,0),(8,24,'Solid Yoke DC Motor','unnamed.jpg',NULL,NULL,0,'motor/dc-motor/solid-yoke-dc-motor','en',NULL,0,0),(9,3,'DC Motor 3',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'motor/dc-motor/dc-motor-3','en',NULL,0,0),(11,22,'Squirrel Cage Motor IE2 Efficiency','unnamed.jpg',NULL,NULL,0,'motor/low-voltage-ac-motor/squirrel-cage-motor-ie2-efficiency','en',NULL,0,0),(12,22,'Squirrel Cage Motor IE3 Efficiency','unnamed.jpg',NULL,NULL,0,'motor/low-voltage-ac-motor/squirrel-cage-motor-ie3-efficiency','en',NULL,0,0),(13,22,'Squirrel Cage Motor IE4 Efficiency','unnamed.jpg',NULL,NULL,0,'motor/low-voltage-ac-motor/squirrel-cage-motor-ie4-efficiency','en',NULL,0,0),(14,22,'Slip Ring Induction Motors','unnamed.jpg',NULL,NULL,0,'motor/low-voltage-ac-motor/slip-ring-induction-motors','en',NULL,0,0),(15,25,'Safe Area High Voltage AC Motor','unnamed.jpg',NULL,NULL,0,'motor/high-voltage-ac-motors/safe-area-high-voltage-ac-motor','en',NULL,0,0),(16,25,'Hazardous Area High Voltage AC Motor','unnamed.jpg',NULL,NULL,0,'motor/high-voltage-ac-motors/hazardous-area-high-voltage-ac-motor','en',NULL,0,0),(17,11,'Safe Area Squirrel Cage IE2 Motors','unnamed.jpg',NULL,NULL,0,'motor/low-voltage-ac-motor/squirrel-cage-motor-ie2-efficiency/safe-area-squirrel-cage-ie2-motors','en',NULL,0,0),(18,1,'AC Motor1 third leve','unnamed.jpg','Testing',NULL,0,'motor/dc-motor/solid-yoke-dc-motor/ac-motor1-third-leve','en',NULL,0,0),(19,100,'Electric','unnamed.jpg',NULL,NULL,0,'electric','en',NULL,0,0),(20,1,'High Voltage Motors','unnamed.jpg','<p>High-voltage motors from CG Power / Crompton for heavy industry &mdash; 3.3 kV, 6.6 kV, and 11 kV squirrel-cage and slip-ring machines rated from a few hundred kW up to 15 MW. Bombay Engineering Syndicate supplies and supports these for power, cement, steel, and petrochemical clients across Maharashtra and Gujarat.</p>\n<p>HV motors drive the largest loads on a site &mdash; induced- and forced-draught fans, boiler-feed and cooling-water pumps, ball mills, crushers, compressors, and raw-mill drives. They are built with robust stator insulation systems (Class F, VPI treatment), sleeve or anti-friction bearings, and cooling arrangements from TEFC (IC411) to air-to-water heat exchangers (CACW/IC81W) for continuous duty in demanding ambients. Slip-ring versions handle high-inertia loads that need a soft, controlled start.</p>\n<p>Specifying an HV motor is an engineering exercise: system voltage, kW and speed, starting method (DOL, reactor, soft starter, or VFD), the starting torque and inertia of the driven load, bearing and cooling type, terminal-box fault rating, and space-heater and RTD accessories all matter. Share the driven equipment and site conditions and our team will configure the right machine. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Request an HV motor quotation.</a></p>',NULL,1,'motor/high-low-voltage-ac-dc-motors/high-voltage-motors',NULL,NULL,0,1),(21,1,'Low Voltage Motors','unnamed.jpg','<p>Low-voltage three-phase motors from CG Power / Crompton &mdash; the workhorse range up to 1000 V, from 0.37 kW to 630 kW, in IE2, IE3, and IE4 efficiency classes. Bombay Engineering Syndicate stocks and sizes these foot- and flange-mounted TEFC motors for factories, pumping stations, and OEM machinery across India.</p>\n<p>LV induction motors drive almost everything in a plant: centrifugal and positive-displacement pumps, fans and blowers, air compressors, conveyors, crushers, machine tools, and gearboxes. The standard build is a totally enclosed fan-cooled (TEFC, IP55) squirrel-cage motor in cast iron or aluminium, in 2/4/6/8-pole for 3000/1500/1000/750 RPM synchronous speeds, with B3 foot, B5/B14 flange, or combined mounting. Insulation is Class F with Class B temperature rise for long winding life.</p>\n<p>To choose correctly, match kW and RPM to the load, confirm mounting and shaft dimensions, set the enclosure to the environment (IP55 standard, IP56/IP66 for wash-down or dusty sites), and pick the efficiency class &mdash; IE3 is now the regulatory baseline for most ratings. We supply genuine motors with test certificates. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Send your requirement</a> for a same-range recommendation.</p>',NULL,2,'motor/high-low-voltage-ac-dc-motors/low-voltage-motors',NULL,NULL,0,1),(22,1,'Energy Efficient Motors','unnamed.jpg','<p>Energy-efficient motors &mdash; CG Power / Crompton IE3 premium and IE4 super-premium ranges that cut running cost and carbon on continuously operated drives. Bombay Engineering Syndicate helps plants in Mumbai, Ahmedabad, and across India switch to high-efficiency motors and calculate the payback.</p>\n<p>A motor\'s purchase price is a small fraction of its lifetime cost &mdash; energy is typically over 95% of the total for a motor that runs long hours. Moving from an old IE1 motor to IE3 or IE4 can cut losses by 20&ndash;40%, often paying back the price difference in under two years on 4000+ hour duty. IE4 motors use improved electrical steel, more copper, and optimised design to reach super-premium efficiency, and they run cooler and quieter, extending bearing and insulation life. India\'s Minimum Energy Performance Standards now mandate IE3 as the floor for most LV ratings, so efficiency is both compliance and savings.</p>\n<p>We help you compare efficiency classes against your operating hours and electricity tariff, size the replacement to your existing load, and pick the right frame for a drop-in swap. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Ask for an efficiency comparison</a> on your motors and we will show the likely payback.</p>',NULL,3,'motor/high-low-voltage-ac-dc-motors/energy-efficient-motors',NULL,NULL,0,1),(23,1,'Motors for Hazardous Area (LV)','unnamed.jpg','<p>Low-voltage hazardous-area motors from CG Power / Crompton &mdash; flameproof (Ex d), increased-safety (Ex e), and non-sparking (Ex nA) machines certified for gas and dust atmospheres. Bombay Engineering Syndicate supplies these for chemical, pharma, paint, fertiliser, and oil-and-gas plants that need explosion-protected drives.</p>\n<p>Where flammable gases, vapours, or combustible dust can be present, a standard motor is a hazard. Explosion-protected LV motors are built and certified so they cannot ignite the surrounding atmosphere &mdash; flameproof enclosures contain any internal spark, while increased-safety designs eliminate arcing and hot surfaces. Selection is governed by the area classification: Zone 1 or Zone 2 for gases (Zone 21/22 for dust), the gas group (IIA/IIB/IIC), and the temperature class (T1&ndash;T6) that caps the motor\'s surface temperature below the auto-ignition point of the substance present.</p>\n<p>Getting this right is a safety and statutory matter &mdash; the certification (ATEX / IECEx / PESO-CCoE) must match the plant\'s hazardous-area drawing. Share your zone, gas group, and temperature class and we will supply a correctly certified motor with full documentation. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Send your hazardous-area requirement.</a></p>',NULL,4,'motor/high-low-voltage-ac-dc-motors/motors-for-hazardous-area-lv',NULL,NULL,0,1),(24,1,'DC Motors','unnamed.jpg','<p>DC motors from CG Power / Crompton &mdash; shunt, series, and compound-wound machines for applications that demand a wide speed range, high starting torque, and precise control. Bombay Engineering Syndicate supplies and supports DC motors for rolling mills, cranes, hoists, extruders, printing, and test rigs.</p>\n<p>Despite the spread of AC drives, DC motors remain the right answer where the load needs full torque from zero speed, a very wide constant-torque speed range, or the simple, responsive control a DC drive gives. They are common on retrofit and legacy lines, in steel and paper mills, and on winders and traction-type duties. The range covers foot and flange mountings, forced-air or self-ventilated cooling, and tacho or encoder feedback for closed-loop speed regulation, matched to a four-quadrant DC drive where regenerative braking is needed.</p>\n<p>Specifying a DC motor means fixing armature voltage and current, base and top speed, field arrangement (shunt or separately excited), duty, cooling, and feedback device &mdash; and matching it to the thyristor drive. We help configure motor and drive together as one package. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Send your DC drive requirement</a> for a matched proposal.</p>',NULL,6,'motor/high-low-voltage-ac-dc-motors/dc-motors',NULL,NULL,0,1),(25,1,'Motors for Hazardous Areas (HV)','unnamed.jpg','<p>High-voltage hazardous-area motors from CG Power / Crompton &mdash; flameproof and increased-safety HV machines (3.3 kV to 11 kV) certified for gas and dust zones in refineries, petrochemical, fertiliser, and offshore plants. Bombay Engineering Syndicate supplies these explosion-protected large motors with full certification support.</p>\n<p>When a large fan, compressor, or pump sits inside a classified area, the motor must be both high-voltage rated and explosion-protected &mdash; a demanding combination that only purpose-built machines meet. These motors carry Ex d (flameproof) or Ex e / Ex p (increased-safety / pressurised) protection, robust Class F VPI insulation, and cooling arrangements sized for continuous duty, all certified to ATEX, IECEx, or PESO-CCoE. As with any Ex motor, the specification hinges on zone (1 or 2), gas group (IIA/IIB/IIC), and temperature class (T1&ndash;T6), now combined with system voltage and the high kW ratings typical of HV loads.</p>\n<p>These are engineered-to-order machines &mdash; share the driven equipment, area classification, system voltage, and site conditions, and our team will configure and quote a compliant motor with all statutory documentation. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Request an HV hazardous-area motor.</a></p>',NULL,5,'motor/high-low-voltage-ac-dc-motors/motors-for-hazardous-areas-hv',NULL,NULL,0,1),(26,1,'Special Application Motors','unnamed.jpg','<p>Special application motors from CG Power / Crompton &mdash; purpose-designed machines for duties a standard catalogue motor cannot serve: brake motors, roller-table motors, crane and hoist duty, smoke-extraction, sugar-centrifuge, and other tailored designs. Bombay Engineering Syndicate configures and supplies these to your exact duty.</p>\n<p>Many industrial drives fall outside the standard range because of their duty cycle, mechanical arrangement, or environment. Brake motors add a fail-safe electromagnetic brake for cranes, hoists, and positioning. Roller-table and mill-duty motors withstand high radial loads, vibration, and heat in steel plants. High-inertia, high-starting-frequency motors suit centrifuges and presses that start and stop constantly. Smoke-extraction motors are certified to keep running at elevated temperature during a fire. Each is built with the right insulation, bearings, cooling, and protection for its specific job.</p>\n<p>Because these are application-driven, the more you tell us the better the fit &mdash; the machine it drives, the duty cycle (S1 to S10), starts per hour, load inertia, ambient, and any braking or feedback needs. Our engineers translate that into a correct specification. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Describe your application</a> and we will propose the right special-duty motor.</p>',NULL,7,'motor/high-low-voltage-ac-dc-motors/special-application-motors',NULL,NULL,0,1),(27,0,'Motor',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'motor','en',NULL,0,0),(100,0,'Motor','unnamed.jpg','<p>Electric motors for every industrial and commercial application &mdash; browse by voltage class, efficiency rating, or application type. As CG Power / Crompton authorised channel partners since 1957, Bombay Engineering Syndicate supplies genuine motors from fractional horsepower to 15 MW with expert selection support from our Fort, Mumbai and Satellite, Ahmedabad offices.</p>\n<p>The catalogue is organised into three families. <strong>High &amp; Low Voltage AC/DC Motors</strong> cover the workhorses of heavy industry &mdash; squirrel-cage and slip-ring machines, energy-efficient IE2/IE3/IE4 ranges, flameproof and increased-safety motors for hazardous zones, and DC machines for precise torque control. <strong>FHP / Commercial Motors</strong> serve OEM builders and light industry with single-phase, NEMA-frame, and application-specific fractional-HP motors. <strong>Drives &amp; Automation</strong> adds Emotron variable frequency drives and soft starters that cut energy bills and protect the motor.</p>\n<p>Choosing the right motor means matching kW rating, RPM (pole count), mounting (foot/flange B3/B5/B14), duty cycle, ambient temperature, and enclosure (IP55 standard, higher for wet or dusty sites) to the driven load. Tell us the application and we will size it, confirm the efficiency class, and quote genuine stock. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Send a motor inquiry</a> for a free recommendation.</p>',NULL,0,'motor',NULL,NULL,0,1),(101,100,'FHP / Commercial Motors','unnamed.jpg','<p>Fractional-horsepower and commercial motors from CG Power / Crompton for OEM equipment, appliances, and light industry &mdash; single-phase motors, NEMA-frame ranges, cooler and fan motors, and application-specific designs. Bombay Engineering Syndicate is a high-volume FHP supply partner to Indian equipment manufacturers, with custom shaft, mounting, and nameplate options.</p>\n<p>FHP motors &mdash; broadly those below 1 HP, though the commercial range extends higher &mdash; are the small motors built into products: air coolers, exhaust and ventilation fans, pumps, mixers, packaging and textile machines, medical and lab equipment, and countless OEM assemblies. The range spans single-phase types (capacitor-start, capacitor-run, and PSC), NEMA-frame motors for export machinery, and general-purpose rolled-steel and aluminium-body motors, in a wide choice of speeds, mountings, and shaft configurations.</p>\n<p>For OEM buyers the priorities are consistent quality at volume, the exact frame and shaft to drop into an existing design, and reliable delivery. We supply genuine motors with the mounting, shaft extension, winding, and nameplate you specify, and hold fast-moving ratings in stock. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Send your FHP or OEM requirement</a> &mdash; drawings welcome &mdash; for pricing and lead time.</p>',NULL,1,'motor/fhp-commercial-motors','en',NULL,0,1),(102,101,'Single Phase Motors','unnamed.jpg','<p>Single-phase motors from CG Power / Crompton for locations with a domestic or light-commercial 230 V supply &mdash; capacitor-start, capacitor-start-capacitor-run, and permanent-split-capacitor (PSC) types from Bombay Engineering Syndicate. Ideal for pumps, air coolers, fans, small machines, and OEM appliances where three-phase power is unavailable.</p>\n<p>Where only single-phase power exists &mdash; homes, shops, small workshops, and rural sites &mdash; these motors deliver reliable fractional to small-integral HP output. The winding type is chosen by the load: capacitor-start (CS) motors give high starting torque for pumps and compressors; capacitor-start-capacitor-run (CSCR) adds better running efficiency and power factor for continuous duty; PSC motors suit low-starting-torque loads like fans and blowers with quiet, simple operation. Builds include rolled-steel and aluminium bodies, foot and flange mounts, and a range of shaft and speed options.</p>\n<p>To select, match HP and RPM to the load, confirm the starting-torque class the application needs, and set the mounting and shaft. For OEM use we supply to your drawing and nameplate. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Send your single-phase motor requirement</a> for a matched recommendation and price.</p>',NULL,1,'motor/fhp-commercial-motors/single-phase-motors',NULL,NULL,0,1),(103,101,'3 Phase Motors - Rolled Steel Body',NULL,NULL,NULL,2,'motor/fhp-commercial-motors/3-phase-motors-rolled-steel-body',NULL,NULL,0,0),(104,101,'Application Specific Motors','unnamed.jpg','<p>Application-specific FHP and commercial motors from CG Power / Crompton &mdash; motors purpose-wound for a defined job rather than a generic catalogue slot. Bombay Engineering Syndicate supplies these for air coolers, exhaust systems, agricultural equipment, packaging lines, and OEM machinery, built to the exact frame, shaft, and winding required.</p>\n<p>Many products need a motor tuned to their duty &mdash; a specific speed and torque, a particular shaft extension or double shaft, a defined mounting to bolt straight into the assembly, or a winding optimised for the appliance\'s supply and running profile. This range groups those tailored fractional and commercial motors: cooler and blower motors, exhaust-fan motors, small pump and agitator motors, and OEM-specified designs. Because they are matched to the application, they run more efficiently and last longer than a forced-fit standard motor.</p>\n<p>The best results come from sharing the equipment details &mdash; driven load, required speed and torque, mounting and shaft dimensions, supply, and duty cycle. Our engineers translate that into the right specification and, for volume OEM orders, hold the design ready to call off. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Send your application details</a> for a tailored proposal.</p>',NULL,3,'motor/fhp-commercial-motors/application-specific-motors',NULL,NULL,0,1),(105,100,'Drives and Automation','unnamed.jpg','<p>Drives and automation from CG Power &mdash; Emotron variable frequency drives (VFDs) and soft starters that control motor speed, save energy, and protect equipment. Bombay Engineering Syndicate supplies, sizes, and supports these across pumping, HVAC, material handling, and process industries in Mumbai, Ahmedabad, and beyond.</p>\n<p>Running a motor straight across the line wastes energy and hammers the mechanics. A VFD varies motor speed to match the actual demand &mdash; on pumps and fans, where power follows the cube of speed, that means dramatic energy savings, plus soft starting, precise process control, and longer equipment life. A soft starter, by contrast, gives a controlled ramp-up and current limit for loads that run at fixed speed but must not slam on. The range covers general-purpose and heavy-duty VFDs, pump- and flow-optimised drives, compact and solar drives, and digital soft starters with built-in motor protection.</p>\n<p>Correct selection depends on motor kW and current, the load type (variable- or constant-torque), starting duty, and control needs. We help you choose between a VFD and a soft starter, size the unit, and specify braking, filters, and enclosures. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Send your drive requirement</a> for a matched proposal.</p>',NULL,2,'motor/drives-and-automation',NULL,NULL,0,1),(106,105,'Industrial Drives','unnamed.jpg','<p>Emotron industrial drives (VFDs) from CG Power &mdash; FDU and VFX series for general and heavy-duty applications, FlowDrive for pump optimisation, VSS/VSX compact drives, solar VSR drives, and lift-specific DSV/GSV units. Bombay Engineering Syndicate supplies and configures variable-speed control that saves energy, extends equipment life, and sharpens process control across industry.</p>\n<p>A variable frequency drive controls motor speed by varying the frequency and voltage supplied, so the motor runs only as fast as the process needs. On pumps and fans the energy payoff is large &mdash; halving the speed can cut power to roughly an eighth &mdash; while on conveyors, mixers, mills, and machine tools the benefit is smooth starting and accurate speed and torque control with reduced mechanical wear. The Emotron range spans compact drives for simple duties up to heavy-duty VFX units engineered for high-inertia, shock-loaded applications like crushers and rock drills, plus dedicated pump, solar-pumping, and elevator drives.</p>\n<p>Sizing a VFD means matching motor current and kW, the load torque profile, overload and starting duty, and control and braking needs, then adding the right filters and enclosure for the environment. Our team specifies the complete drive package. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Send your VFD requirement.</a></p>',NULL,1,'motor/drives-and-automation/industrial-drives',NULL,NULL,0,1),(107,105,'Soft Starters','unnamed.jpg','<p>Digital soft starters from CG Power / Emotron &mdash; TSA and MSF-series units that give motors a controlled, current-limited start and built-in protection. Bombay Engineering Syndicate supplies and sizes soft starters for pumps, fans, compressors, conveyors, and mills where a smooth start matters but variable speed is not required.</p>\n<p>Starting a motor direct-on-line draws six to eight times full-load current and delivers a mechanical jolt that stresses couplings, belts, gearboxes, and the driven load &mdash; and on pumps it causes damaging pressure surges and water hammer. A soft starter ramps voltage up smoothly, limiting inrush current and torque, then (on advanced units) switches to an internal bypass for loss-free running. Many models add electronic overload, phase-loss, and stall protection, plus a soft-stop feature that eases pumps down to prevent hammer. Where the load runs at fixed speed, a soft starter delivers most of the mechanical benefit of a VFD at lower cost.</p>\n<p>Selection depends on motor kW and current, the start duty and starts per hour, and the load type. We help you decide between a soft starter and a VFD and size the unit correctly. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Send your soft-starter requirement.</a></p>',NULL,2,'motor/drives-and-automation/soft-starters',NULL,NULL,0,1),(108,101,'NEMA Frame Motors',NULL,'<p>NEMA-frame motors from CG Power / Crompton &mdash; motors built to the North American NEMA dimensional and performance standard for export machinery sold into US and NEMA-market territories. Bombay Engineering Syndicate supplies these to Indian OEMs and exporters who need NEMA-compliant drives on their products.</p>\n<p>NEMA and IEC are the two global motor standards, and they differ in frame dimensions, mounting, output markings (HP vs kW), and design designations (NEMA Design A/B/C/D torque curves). Machinery destined for the United States, Canada, and other NEMA markets generally must use NEMA-frame motors so that dimensions, terminal arrangements, and performance meet buyer and code expectations. This range provides those motors &mdash; correct NEMA frame sizes, foot and C-face mountings, 60 Hz and dual-frequency windings, and the ratings export equipment builders ask for.</p>\n<p>If you are building for export, tell us the NEMA frame, HP, voltage/frequency, enclosure (ODP/TEFC), and mounting your customer specifies, and we will supply compliant motors with documentation. Unsure whether you need NEMA or IEC? We will help you confirm. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Send your export motor requirement.</a></p>',NULL,0,'motor/fhp-commercial-motors/nema-frame-motors',NULL,NULL,0,1),(109,101,'General Purpose Body Motors',NULL,'<p>General-purpose body motors from CG Power / Crompton &mdash; standard rolled-steel and aluminium-body FHP and commercial motors for everyday industrial and OEM use. Bombay Engineering Syndicate stocks these versatile, economical motors for pumps, fans, machines, and equipment across Mumbai, Ahmedabad, and pan-India.</p>\n<p>These are the general-duty motors that fit the majority of light-industrial and OEM needs without special features &mdash; a reliable, cost-effective drive for a broad range of loads. Rolled-steel-body construction keeps them light and economical for appliances and mass-produced equipment, while the range offers the common speeds (2/4/6-pole), foot and flange mountings, and standard shaft sizes that most machines are designed around. TEFC enclosures suit typical indoor and sheltered environments, and IP protection can be stepped up where conditions demand.</p>\n<p>Because they are standard, these motors are usually available from stock and quick to supply for repairs, retrofits, and production runs alike. To choose, match HP and RPM to the driven load and confirm mounting and shaft; step up to a special or application-specific motor only if the duty or environment is unusual. <a href=\"/product-inquiry/\">Send your requirement</a> and we will confirm the right general-purpose motor and its availability.</p>',NULL,0,'motor/fhp-commercial-motors/general-purpose-body-motors',NULL,NULL,0,1);
